      "problem": "The surface area of a cube is $294\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Find the length of the edges of the cube.",
      "worked_solution": "The surface area $S$ of a cube is made up of $6$ congruent squares. So, the area $A$ of one face is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{S}{6}=\\frac{294}{6}=49\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nSince $A={s}^{2},$ where $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt{A}=\\sqrt{49}=7\\,\\text{cm}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $7\\,\\text{cm}.$",
